menu "My UPS Pal web page"

config UPSA_SETUP_SCREEN
    bool "Show the guided Wi-Fi setup screen on a board with no network"
    default y
    help
        With this on (the upstream behaviour), a board that has not joined a
        network shows nothing but the Wi-Fi card: the menu, the status and
        every other card are hidden until it joins one. That is right when the
        network IS the product -- the board is useless until it is on one.

        Turn it OFF for a board whose network is optional. This adapter sends
        its UPS data over RS485 and most units never join a Wi-Fi at all; the
        radio exists so a technician can open the page. Leaving the guided
        screen on would leave those boards behind a Wi-Fi form for their whole
        service life, with no way to reach anything else.

        Off, the page comes up normally on the board's own access point and
        Wi-Fi is one ordinary card among the others, there if it is wanted.

endmenu
